<figure id="S5.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="S5.F4.3" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;"><img src="2509.12522v1/Project_Images/q-norm-history.png" id="S5.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:229/236;" width="229" height="236" alt="Refer to caption">
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="S5.F4.4" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;"><img src="2509.12522v1/Project_Images/CP-empirical-coverage-compare.png" id="S5.F4.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:229/236;" width="229" height="236" alt="Refer to caption">
</div></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S5.F4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Quantile norm and empirical coverage dynamics plots for the marginal CP-augmented PI-AttNP and joint CP-augmented PI-AttNP approaches. Note that for the coverage plot on the right, quantiles for model uncertainty <math id="S5.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> were computed based on <math id="S5.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.05</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{D}_{\text{cal}}|=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>cal</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{D}_{\text{cal}}|=1000</annotation></semantics></math>. Given samples <math id="S5.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},y_{i})\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>cal</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},y_{i})\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote coverage <math id="S5.F4.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=\;(|y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(x_{i})|\;/\;|\mathcal{D}_{\text{cal}}|)\times 100\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.058em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.280em">/</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>cal</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>100</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\;(|y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(x_{i})|\;/\;|\mathcal{D}_{\text{cal}}|)\times 100\%</annotation></semantics></math>. For CP-marginal, the coverage computed for each individual state was averaged together to get the scalar value observed in the plot.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
