<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="S5.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">X-direction translational velocity and acceleration <math id="S5.F5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{x}^{I},a_{x}^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{x}^{I},a_{x}^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> (first column) along with X-direction rotational velocity and acceleration <math id="S5.F5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{x},\dot{\omega}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">˙</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{x},\dot{\omega}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> state trajectory comparisons to ground-truth (black) between the PI-AttNP (blue) w/ marginal CP-based confidence bounds <math id="S5.F5.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pm q_{\alpha}\cdot\hat{\sigma}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm q_{\alpha}\cdot\hat{\sigma}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> (dotted-blue), AttNP (yellow) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2019)</a></cite>, Deep Kalman Filter (red) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al. (2024)</a></cite>, PINN-LSTM (green) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">de Curtò and de Zarzà (2024)</a></cite>, and hand-tuned covariance UKF (magenta). Note that perturbation parameters used above are <math id="S5.F5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{w}=50\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;-1&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\;m/s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{w}=50\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;-1&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\;m/s</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.F5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta\bar{\omega}_{\text{max}}|=200\;rad/s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">¯</mo></mover><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>200</mn><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta\bar{\omega}_{\text{max}}|=200\;rad/s</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe numerical results of all models in Table <a href="#S5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 5.5 Convergence Dynamics ‣ 5 Results and Validation ‣ Hybrid State Estimation of Uncertain Nonlinear Dynamics Using Neural Processes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, and observe the remaining state trajectory plots in the Y/Z directions in Figure <a href="#S7.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 7.3 Noise Generation Implementation for 𝜉_𝑘 ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Hybrid State Estimation of Uncertain Nonlinear Dynamics Using Neural Processes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
